      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes the stale CMake CUDA compiler gates reported in #65440 to prevent source build failures when targeting CUDA 12.6.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Raises `cooperative_topk` CUDA compiler gate from 12.0 to 12.8, matching CCCL async-bulk and mbarrier API requirements.\n- Raises DeepGEMM SM90 CUDA compiler gate from 12.3 to 12.9, matching `compatibility.hpp` static assertions.\n\n## Validation\n\n- On CUDA compiler versions < 12.8, `cooperative_topk` is bypassed cleanly instead of raising CCCL overload errors.\n- On CUDA compiler versions < 12.9, DeepGEMM gracefully falls back to the stub `_deep_gemm_C` target instead of failing the static assertion.\n\n## Details\n\n1. `csrc/cooperative_topk.cuh` invokes `cuda::ptx::mbarrier_try_wait_parity` and `cuda::ptx::cp_async_bulk`, introduced in CUDA 12.8 CCCL. The existing gate of 12.0 caused build failures on CUDA 12.6.\n2. DeepGEMM's `csrc/utils/compatibility.hpp` static-asserts `CUDA_VERSION >= 12090`. Raising the CMake gate from 12.3 to 12.9 ensures the stub target is selected on CUDA < 12.9.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality.\n</details>",
